  o Minor bugfixes (buffers):
    - When scanning a buffer for a string, such as the end of an HTTP
      header, skip chunks that contain no data instead of comparing
      against bytes past the end of a chunk. Previously a buffer ending
      in a partial CRLF at a chunk boundary could be treated as a
      finished header and rejected, and a delimiter split by an empty
      chunk could be missed. Fixes bug 41377; bugfix on 0.2.0.16-alpha.
